<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Template, not the installed file. {{HOME}} and {{REPO}} are substituted on
  install; see the "Screen time and sleep" step in AGENTS.md. launchd does not
  expand ~ or $HOME, so every path here has to be absolute.

  Three chances a day to collect, rather than one, because the Mac is the only
  machine that can read knowledgeC.db and Biome and both are pruned to roughly
  four weeks — a night the laptop was shut is a night of history that no later
  run can recover:

    - RunAtLoad, so a Mac that was off through both slots collects at the next
      login instead of waiting for tomorrow;
    - 12:00, which catches a laptop that was closed at 23:00 the night before;
    - 23:00, the real one, late enough to have most of the day in it.

  Running repeatedly is free: write_habit merges, so the noon run's partial day
  is simply overwritten by the fuller number at 23:00, and habits_daily.py
  skips the commit entirely when no day changed.

  The interpreter is /usr/bin/python3, and the Full Disk Access grant has to be
  on that exact path. It is worth knowing that /usr/bin/python3 is a stub —
  the same inode as /usr/bin/git, one of 78 hard links — which hands off to the
  Command Line Tools interpreter, and an earlier version of this file argued
  from that fact that a grant on it could never apply. That is not what this
  machine does. TCC keys the decision to the path launchd is told to execute:

    - /Library/Application Support/com.apple.TCC/TCC.db lists /usr/bin/python3
      as allowed for kTCCServiceSystemPolicyAllFiles, and has no row of any
      kind for the Command Line Tools binary;
    - pointed at /usr/bin/python3 the agent read knowledgeC.db every night
      through 2026-09-02; pointed at the CLT binary on 2026-09-03 it failed
      twice in a row with "cannot open knowledgeC.db (authorization denied)".

  So grant Full Disk Access to /usr/bin/python3 and nothing else. Re-check with
  the sqlite3 query above rather than from memory if it ever fails again — the
  grant is per-binary, and the symptom of granting the wrong one is a bare
  "authorization denied" that names no path.

  EnvironmentVariables/PATH is not optional. launchd starts jobs with
  PATH=/usr/bin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/sbin, which does not contain git-lfs
  (/opt/homebrew/bin/git-lfs). This repo tracks PDFs through LFS and .git/hooks/
  pre-push tests for the binary with `command -v git-lfs`, so without Homebrew
  on PATH every push aborts in the hook: the run commits, logs "push failed ...
  'git-lfs' was not found on your path", and nothing reaches GitHub.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>Label</key>
  <string>com.owenmedeiros.habits</string>

  <key>ProgramArguments</key>
  <array>
    <string>/usr/bin/python3</string>
    <string>{{REPO}}/scripts/habits_daily.py</string>
  </array>

  <key>EnvironmentVariables</key>
  <dict>
    <key>PATH</key>
    <string>/opt/homebrew/bin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/sbin</string>
  </dict>

  <key>RunAtLoad</key>
  <true/>

  <key>StartCalendarInterval</key>
  <array>
    <dict>
      <key>Hour</key>
      <integer>12</integer>
      <key>Minute</key>
      <integer>0</integer>
    </dict>
    <dict>
      <key>Hour</key>
      <integer>23</integer>
      <key>Minute</key>
      <integer>0</integer>
    </dict>
  </array>

  <key>StandardOutPath</key>
  <string>{{HOME}}/Library/Logs/habits-daily.log</string>
  <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
  <string>{{HOME}}/Library/Logs/habits-daily.log</string>
</dict>
</plist>
